<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chandela dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">831 CE – 1315 CE (approx.) · capital Khajuraho</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Rajput dynasty of Bundelkhand that built the temples of Khajuraho, famous for their carved sculpture.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nannuka">Nannuka</a> founded the Chandela line around 831 as a feudatory of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gurjara-pratihara">Gurjara-Pratihara</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jejakabhukti">Jejakabhukti</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-chandela">Yashovarman</a> made the dynasty a regional power in the mid-10th century, capturing the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinjar-fort">Kalinjar</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhanga">Dhanga</a> became fully independent.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Chandelas built some 85 temples at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a> between about 950 and 1050, of which about 25 survive, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmana-temple-khajuraho">Lakshmana temple</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yashovarman-chandela">Yashovarman</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandariya-mahadeva-temple">Kandariya Mahadeva</a>. They were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> but also supported Jain temples. Their kingdom was held by great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinjar-fort">Kalinjar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajaigarh">Ajaygarh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahoba">Mahoba</a> and watered by large artificial lakes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidyadhara-chandela-dynasty">Vidyadhara</a> resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> in the early 11th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraja III</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chahamanas-of-shakambhari">Chahamanas of Shakambhari</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paramardi">Paramardi</a> in 1182, and in 1203 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutb-ud-din-aibak">Qutb al-Din Aibak</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinjar-fort">Kalinjar</a>. The Chandelas survived as a local power until about 1315.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chandela-dynasty.jpg" alt="Chandela dynasty" width="320" height="159"><figcaption>Image: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandelas_of_Jejakabhukti._Sallakshana_Varman._Circa_1120-1135_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>831 CE – 1315 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Khajuraho</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yashovarman, Dhanga, Vidyadhara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chandelas of Jejakabhukti, Chandellas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1073&amp;focus=chandela-dynasty" aria-label="Chandela dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6801 1263 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chandela dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7121 1519L7103 1442M7121 1519L7018 1385"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7103 1442h0M7018 1385h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7121 1519h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7121 1519h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Khajuraho. <a href="/atlas?year=1073&amp;focus=chandela-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

